		<Lockup id="backend" index={5} number="05" label="Under the hood" title="There is no public API." dim="So it reads what the official app reads."
			deepDive="Deep dive: how the map was drawn" next={{ label: 'Next: signing in with CIE', href: '#cie' }}
			facts={[{ label: 'Service config', value: '200', note: 'public, no sign-in' }, { label: 'Path exists', value: '401', accent: true }, { label: 'Path gone', value: '404' }]}
			factsNote="Probed 11 September 2026">
			The official web app is a public single-page app, and its bundle carries the route table and every path. On launch the official app fetches <b>one unauthenticated config with every backend’s address</b>. PoliVerse reads the same config, with the current hosts compiled in as fallbacks, so <b>a backend that moves costs a fetch, not a release</b>.
			<Fragment slot="deep-dive"><p>No proxy and no TLS interception: the web bundle, about 8 MB, is served to anyone who asks. Each path found in it was then probed without credentials. A 401 means the path exists and wants a token; a 404 means it is gone.</p></Fragment>
		</Lockup>

